    <strong>Chapter 10: Data Manipulation</strong>
</div>

<div style="text-align:center; font-size:28px; font-weight:bold;">
    Data Extraction in Pandas
</div>
<br>
<div style="font-size:18px;">

Using the DataFrame loaded from `'data/patient_records.csv'` which contains columns **'Patient_ID'**, **'Age'**, **'Blood_Pressure'**, **'Cholesterol'**, **'Weight'**, and **'Height'**, complete the following tasks:

# Question 1
- Extract the **'Age'** column as a Series. Print its type and first 3 values.

<span style="color:#8b0153;">Hint</span>: Use single brackets for Series extraction
<br></br>

# Question 2
- Create a new DataFrame containing only the **'Blood_Pressure'** and **'Cholesterol'** columns.

<span style="color:#8b0153;">Hint</span>: Use double brackets for DataFrame extraction
<br></br>

# Question 3
- Extract data for patients **'P001'** to **'P003'** using `.loc[]`.

<span style="color:#8b0153;">Hint</span>: Remember `.loc[]` is inclusive
<br></br>

# Question 4
- Extract the first three rows of the DataFrame using `.iloc[]`.

<span style="color:#8b0153;">Hint</span>: Remember `.iloc[]` is exclusive
<br></br>

# Question 5
- Extract rows 2-4 and columns **'Height'** and **'Weight'** using `.iloc[]`.

<span style="color:#8b0153;">Hint</span>: Use slicing for both rows and columns

<br></br>
</div>